# The repository's line endings are part of its contract, not a local preference.
#
# `daoris.lock` records a sha256 per installed document and `check` compares against it, so what a
# document's bytes ARE has to be the same everywhere. Without this file that depends on each
# developer's global `core.autocrlf`: a Windows clone gets CRLF working files, a Linux clone LF, and
# the same repository disagrees with itself about its own doctrine.
#
# Both halves of the tool normalize on read, so this is the belt to that suspenders — but a hash
# authority should not rest on every reader remembering to normalize.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A vendor's release files, kept byte for byte (AGT2b): a signature and a published hash speak for
# exact bytes, and a normalized fixture would fail its own verification for a reason that is ours.
src/Daoris.Cli/test/fixtures/vendor/** -text

# Written by `daoris sync`, which writes LF atomically. Never a merge conflict worth resolving by
# hand: regenerate it instead.
daoris.lock -merge

# Written by `tools/orient-index.mjs` from the tree (ORIENT1a), its line numbers moving with nearly every
# change. A textual merge of two copies is neither copy's tree, so none is attempted: `tools/merge-branch.mjs`
# writes the folder again from the merged tree, and a hand merge runs the tool.
docs/index/** -merge

# The append-only records merge by union (MOD1, D106): every branch adds lines at one insertion point,
# and nothing about the work collides, only the place. Union keeps both sides' lines. It also keeps both
# versions of a line two branches changed, so `tools/doc-duplicates.mjs` (run by `verify`) refuses a
# decision number, heading, index row or changelog line that appears twice; the parent reads every
# merged diff besides. Not the backlog: rows move out of it, which union would undo.
#
# The decisions are one file per decision, each merged by union on its own (D134): as one file, union put
# a note under the wrong decision or a decision in twice in a quarter of its merges. The page left at
# `docs/DECISIONS.md` is not union-merged, so a note a branch from before wrote there conflicts, and the
# check refuses one that lands.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/decisions/*.md merge=union
docs/task-archive.md merge=union
docs/FIX-LOG.md merge=union
docs/README.md merge=union
.claude/knowledge/twins.md merge=union
